SUMMARY:3VB University of Cambridge Event
LOCATION:Downing College
URL:https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/3vb-university-cambridge-event
CATEGORIES:Law,International
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nTopics: Law\, International\nDetails: https://w
 ww.law.cam.ac.uk/events/3vb-university-cambridge-event\nDate/time: \n\n Th
 ursday 26 November 2026 \n\n 5:00pm to 6:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Downing C
 ollege\n\n West Lodge & Maitland Room\n\n About \n\n Following a brief int
 roduction by 3VB's Rajesh Pillai KC\, members of 3VB will offer first-hand
  insights into two recent landmark cases\, exploring how legal decisions a
 re reached and the role of barristers in shaping them.\n Dominic Kennelly 
 will discuss Spain v Infrastructure Services Luxembourg [2026] UKSC 9\, co
 ncerning state immunity and the enforcement of international arbitration a
 wards\, while William Day and Amelia-Rose Edwards will explore Gatwick Inv
 estment Ltd v Liberty Mutual Insurance Europe SE [2026] UKSC 14\, addressi
 ng contractual interpretation and causation in private law.\n The talks wi
 ll be followed by drinks\, refreshments and an opportunity to network with
  members of Chambers.\n RSVP: events@3vb.com \n\n Contact \n\n Email: even
 ts@3vb.com
END:VEVENT
